    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0606",
      "reading_order": 925,
      "section": "Water requiremts for closed water circuits",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 63.609700000000004,
        "t": 751.6809000000001,
        "r": 530.8753999999993,
        "b": 685.9241
      },
      "content": "The use of a closed water circuit minimises make-up water requirements. Therefore, the use of soft or even demineralised water is economically feasible and eliminates the problem of scale deposits. Although the heat exchanger is made of stainless steel, the water circuit connected to the compressor may require corrosion inhibitors. Consult section Cooling water requirements to minimise problems due to bad water quality. If in any doubt, consult  Atlas Copco.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_924",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5       Energy recovery (optional)"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_924",
          "title": "Water requiremts for closed water circuits"
        }
      ],
      "page": 88,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0607",
      "reading_order": 926,
      "section": "Water requiremts for closed water circuits",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 63.6105,
        "t": 678.5409,
        "r": 517.4286999999995,
        "b": 653.1638999999999
      },
      "content": "Add an anti-freeze product such as ethylene-glycol to the water in proportion to the expected temperature to avoid freezing.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_924",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
