    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0614",
      "reading_order": 933,
      "section": "Detailed description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 63.609699999999975,
        "t": 429.06100000000004,
        "r": 539.1330999999988,
        "b": 377.88460000000003
      },
      "content": "Bypass valve (BV2) is integrated in the ER unit and controls the working of the oil/water heat exchanger (HE) of the ER unit. Bypass valve (BV1) is integrated in the oil filter housing of the compressor and controls the working of the main oil cooler (Co) of the compressor. Both bypass valves consist of an insert (thermostat) mounted in a housing. Bypass valve BV2 has a separate housing, while BV1 is integrated in the oil filter housing.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_932",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
